<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Babiito dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Babito, Bito dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Babiito are the ruling dynasty of the Kingdom of Bunyoro-Kitara in western Uganda. According to tradition they were Luo-speaking newcomers from the north who succeeded the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chwezi">Chwezi</a> around 1500. Branches of the dynasty ruled other kingdoms of the region, including Kiziba and later Toro, and the omukama of Bunyoro still comes from the family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/babiito-dynasty.jpg" alt="Babiito dynasty" width="320" height="604" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wissenschaftler-Uni · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wappen_Bunyoro.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
